<doc id="176512" url="https://jv.wikipedia.org/wiki?curid=176512" title="Ching bo leung">
Ching bo leung

Ching bo tangan (Chinese ; uga dieja ching po tangan utawa qing bu liang) yaiku sup sing asale saka &lt;a href="Masakan%20Cinten"&gt;Cina kanthi&lt;/a&gt; asri lan umume disajikake ing masakan Kanton, masakan Hainan lan masakan Guangxi. &lt;a href="Tong%20sui"&gt;Yaiku jinise tong sui&lt;/a&gt;. Dikenal kanthi jeneng sâm bổ lượng utawa chè sâm bổ lượng (&lt;a href="Ch%C3%A8"&gt;chè sing&lt;/a&gt; artine "sup manis") ing Vietnam.
Sanajan resep sing tepat bisa beda-beda, omben kasebut umume ngemot biji-bijian &lt;a href="Jali"&gt;yi mai&lt;/a&gt; (gandum mutiara Tionghoa), &lt;a href="Kl%C3%A8ngk%C3%A8ng"&gt;rindu&lt;/a&gt; garing, jujubes abang, wiji teraté, lan &lt;a href="Gulma%20segara"&gt;rumput laut sing&lt;/a&gt; diiris tipis, kanthi banyu, gula, lan es sing diremuk. Minangka panggonane yi mai, barley mutiara bisa uga digunakake, lan irisan &lt;a href="Ja%C3%A9"&gt;jahe&lt;/a&gt; lan / utawa oyod ginseng sing tipis, &lt;a href="Goji%20beri"&gt;wolfberry&lt;/a&gt;, utawa kacang ginkgo bisa uga katon minangka bahan.
Wangun inum saka Cina, ching bo tangan, sing paling populer ing &lt;a href="Olahan%20Kanton"&gt;masakan Kanton&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="Guangdong"&gt;ing Guangdong&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Hong%20Kong"&gt;Hong Kong&lt;/a&gt;, lan &lt;a href="Makau"&gt;Macau&lt;/a&gt;. Kadang dikenal minangka &lt;a href="Sop%20ing%20Asia%20Wetan"&gt;sup Luk mei&lt;/a&gt; (六味 湯, surem. Enem sup rasa). Versi Vietnam, sâm bổ lượng, paling gampang kasedhiya ing &lt;a href="Cholon%2C%20Kota%20Ho%20Chi%20Minh"&gt;Cholon&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Pecinan"&gt;Chinatown&lt;/a&gt; saka &lt;a href="Kutha%20Ho%20Chi%20Minh"&gt;Hồ Chí Minh City&lt;/a&gt;, lan umume disajikake ing gelas dhuwur. Sanajan asring diandharake minangka omben-omben, tembung "sup" luwih cocog amarga sendok umume dibutuhake kanggo ngonsumsi bahan-bahan padhet.
