Cozido à portuguesa

Cozido à portuguesa (pronounced [kuˈziðu a puɾtuˈɣeza]) or Portuguese stew is a type of &lt;a href="Cocido"&gt;cozido&lt;/a&gt;, traditional Portuguese boiled meal. Numerous regional variations exist throughout &lt;a href="Portegal"&gt;Portugal&lt;/a&gt;, and the dish is considered part of the &lt;a href="Masakan%20Portugis"&gt;Portuguese&lt;/a&gt; heritage, as well as one of the &lt;a href="Olahan%20nasional"&gt;national dishes&lt;/a&gt; of Portugal.
Cozido à portuguesa disiapake kanthi akeh sayuran (&lt;a href="Brassica%20oleracea"&gt;kubis&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Buncis"&gt;kacang buncis&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Kenthang"&gt;kentang&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Wortel%20jangan"&gt;wortel&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="turnip"&gt;turnip&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Pantun"&gt;beras&lt;/a&gt;), daging (daging &lt;a href="Iwak%20pitik"&gt;pitik&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Iga%20babi"&gt;tulang rusuk&lt;/a&gt; &lt;a href="Daging%20bakon"&gt;daging babi&lt;/a&gt;, daging &lt;a href="Kuping%20babi"&gt;babi, kuping&lt;/a&gt; daging babi lan &lt;a href="Sikil%20babi"&gt;trotters&lt;/a&gt;, macem-macem bagian &lt;a href="P%C3%A9rangan%20daging%20sapi"&gt;daging sapi&lt;/a&gt;), lan &lt;a href="Sosis"&gt;sosis asap&lt;/a&gt; (&lt;a href="Chorizo"&gt;chouriço&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="farinheira"&gt;farinheira&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href="Sosis%20getih"&gt;morcela&lt;/a&gt;, lan &lt;a href="sosis%20getih"&gt;sosis getih&lt;/a&gt;), lan liya-liyane. Rempah-rempah tradhisional dibumbui nganggo pasta mrica abang, mrica &lt;a href="Mrica"&gt;putih&lt;/a&gt; lan &lt;a href="Kayu%20legi"&gt;kayu manis&lt;/a&gt;. 
